FAQ = [
 ("Why do so many JL liners exclude the 4xe?",
  "The Wrangler 4xe plug-in hybrid carries its battery pack under the rear seat, which changes the rear floor area. 3W, LASFIT and Falafa all list their Unlimited sets as not for the 4xe. If you have a 4xe, look for a listing that names it or ask the seller about the rear piece; the front floor is the same as other JLs."),
 ("Do JK Wrangler liners fit a JL?",
  "Mostly not. The JL (2018+) replaced the JK with a new body and interior. Husky does list its 13021 front pair for 2018–2026 JK/JL and 2020–2026 Gladiator, because the 2018 model year overlapped both generations and the front footwell is similar. But full sets are generation-specific: Husky's 93971 is for 2007–2018 JK Unlimited, while its 93921 is for the JL Unlimited."),
 ("What's the difference between 2-door and Unlimited liners?",
  "The rear floor. The 2-door has a short rear area; the 4-door Unlimited has a full rear footwell. Husky sells the 93991 for the JL 2-door and the 93921 for the Unlimited. Budget brands on this page are Unlimited only."),
 ("What does 'with subwoofer' mean on a Wrangler cargo liner?",
  "JLs with the premium Alpine audio have a subwoofer in the cargo area, which changes the cargo floor shape. 3W sells two floor-plus-cargo kits, one for trucks with the subwoofer and one without. Look in the cargo area for a speaker enclosure before choosing."),
 ("Does the JL have floor drain plugs?",
  "Wranglers are designed to be opened up, and the JL tub has drain plugs in the floor so you can wash out the interior. Liners with high walls keep most water and mud off the carpet in the first place, which means you use the drain plugs less. If you remove the carpet entirely, a nibbed liner will grip the bare floor less well, so rely on the retention posts."),
 ("Do Gladiator liners fit a Wrangler?",
  "The front pair can: Husky's 13021 front liners are listed for both. The rear floors are different, since the Gladiator is a truck with its own cab and rear seat. Buy a rear or full set that names your vehicle."),
 ("Are Rubicon and 392 liners different?",
  "No. Trims don't change the floor. The Rubicon 392 is a 4-door Unlimited, so Unlimited sets fit. The 4xe is the one powertrain that changes the rear floor."),
 ("How should the driver liner sit?",
  "Flat, hooked onto the retention posts, and clear of the pedals at full travel. Remove the factory mat first. On manual-transmission JLs, check the clutch pedal travel too."),
 ("How do I clean liners after the trail?",
  "Pull them, hose them and scrub with mild soap. Let them dry before reinstalling. Skip silicone protectants, which make the surface slick under wet boots."),
 ("Should I add a cargo liner?",
  "On a JL, yes if you carry gear. The cargo area is small and gets muddy quickly. Match the cargo liner to whether you have the subwoofer and whether you have a 4xe."),
 ("Will a liner interfere with the JL's manual transmission clutch?",
  "A liner cut for the JL follows the footwell, and the JL's six-speed manual uses the same front floor shape as far as the listings on this page indicate. Husky's 13021 front pair and its full sets don't split by transmission for the JL. After installing, press the clutch to the floor and make sure it doesn't touch the liner edge. If it does, the liner isn't seated on the retention posts."),
]

